mounted (a constructor) for calling the function

Axios is a JavaScript library used to communicate with APIs.
Methods

Methods contain functions that perform actions.

| Vue Concept              | Meaning                         |
| ------------------------ | ------------------------------- |
| `new Vue()`              | Creates a Vue application       |
| `el`                     | Connects Vue to HTML            |
| `data`                   | Stores application data         |
| `methods`                | Stores functions                |
| `mounted()`              | Runs after Vue loads            |
| `{{ }}`                  | Displays data                   |
| `v-model`                | Two-way data binding            |
| `v-for`                  | Loops through data              |
| `v-if`                   | Conditionally displays elements |
| `@click`                 | Handles a click                 |
| `@submit`                | Handles form submission         |
| `.prevent`               | Prevents default browser action |
| `this`                   | Refers to the Vue instance      |
| `axios.get()`            | Gets data from an API           |
| `async`                  | Defines asynchronous function   |
| `await`                  | Waits for asynchronous result   |
| `localStorage.setItem()` | Saves browser data              |
| `localStorage.getItem()` | Retrieves browser data          |
